# Everything here is sent to the Docker daemon as build context before a single
# instruction runs. Without this file the context was 282 MB, of which 277 MB
# was `.venv` — copied over the wire on every build, on a NAS that has to do
# that build itself. The Dockerfile only ever COPYs ct/, db/, migrations/,
# config/, alembic.ini and pyproject.toml, so none of it was reachable anyway.

# Local virtualenv and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Runtime state, none of which belongs in an image
data/
logs/
state/
backups/
reports/
models/

# Secrets. These are mounted as Docker secrets at run time and must never be
# baked into a layer — an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull it.
secrets/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Version control and editor noise
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs are not needed to run the engine. ARCHITECTURE.md alone is 61 KB and
# changes often, which would bust the cache layer on every edit.
*.md
!README.md
